# Constants a vendored YNL spec gets wrong, excused by name from the spec/header
# comparison in scripts/audit_uapi_constants.py (#167). Each needs a reason.
#
# Keep this short: a disagreement is, by default, a bug in the derivation or in
# nlink. Only list a name after checking which side is right.

# nlctrl.yaml lists `mask` before `pad` in policy-attrs. netlink.h, which owns
# these, has NL_POLICY_TYPE_ATTR_PAD = 11 and NL_POLICY_TYPE_ATTR_MASK = 12 (pad
# was added first, in 5.8; mask after it). The spec is a description of the
# header and has the order wrong.
NL_POLICY_TYPE_ATTR_MASK
NL_POLICY_TYPE_ATTR_PAD
